  "messages": [
    {
      "content": "Solve this problem step by step. Put your final answer within \\boxed{}.\n\nWhat annual interest rate does Jane's savings account offer? Jane has saved $5 from her allowance every week for the past 8 weeks. Jane will continue saving the same amount every two weeks. Jane keeps her allowance savings in an account that pays 2% annual interest. The account compounds interest once at the end of each year.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "EXACT PUBLIC STATE AFTER TURN 6; NO PRIVATE OR FUTURE DATA\nPUBLIC_STATE_JSON:\n{\"completed_task_turns\":[{\"turn\":1,\"user_message\":\"Solve this problem step by step. Put your final answer within \\\\boxed{}.\\n\\nWhat annual interest rate does Jane's savings account offer? Jane has saved $5 from her allowance every week for the past 8 weeks. Jane will continue saving the same amount every two weeks. Jane keeps her allowance savings in an account that pays 2% annual interest. The account compounds interest once at the end of each year.\"},{\"turn\":2,\"user_message\":\"Wait, I made a mistake. Jane has saved $4 from her allowance every week for the past 8 weeks.\"},{\"turn\":3,\"user_message\":\"Actually, that was wrong. Jane will continue saving the same amount each week.\"},{\"turn\":4,\"user_message\":\"Oh, I forgot to mention: Jane's allowance savings are measured in dollars per week.\"},{\"turn\":5,\"user_message\":\"Great. Now let's take that a step further. How much money will Jane have saved from her allowance after one full year? Also, here's some more context: Jane saves money for 52 weeks in a year. This calculation ignores any interest earned in the account.\"},{\"turn\":6,\"user_message\":\"Here's another detail: Her weekly saving rate is constant throughout the year.\"}],\"public_metadata\":{\"benchmark\":\"Evolving Intent GSM8K\",\"upstream_commit\":\"993d6be9597ac03854b46362ccd647eb1bfd267a\"}}",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Good, now using that, can you calculate: How many more weeks will Jane need to save to have a total savings of $60? By the way, Jane wants to have saved a total of $60.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Jane saves **$4 per week**.\n\n1. Amount already saved after 8 weeks:\n   \\[\n   8 \\times \\$4=\\$32\n   \\]\n\n2. Amount still needed:\n   \\[\n   \\$60-\\$32=\\$28\n   \\]\n\n3. Number of additional weeks:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{\\$28}{\\$4\\text{/week}}=7\\text{ weeks}\n   \\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{7\\text{ more weeks}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    }
  ],
